{"id":"laban","name":"Laban","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:laban"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Laban","text":"White. (1.) The son of Bethuel, who was the son of Nahor, Abraham’s brother. He lived at Haran in Mesopotamia. His sister Rebekah was Isaac’s wife (Gen. 24). Jacob, one of the sons of this marriage, fled to the house of Laban, whose daughters Leah and Rachel (ch. 29) he eventually married. (See JACOB.) (2.) A city in the Arabian desert in the route of the Israelites (Deut. 1:1), probably identical with Libnah (Num. 33:20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3837","lemma":"לָבָן","xlit":"Lâbân","gloss":"Laban, a Mesopotamian","kjv":"Laban","count":36,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","xlit":"Yaʻăqôb","gloss":"Jaakob, the Israelitish patriarch","kjv":"Jacob","count":37,"share":0.37},{"strong":"H7354","lemma":"רָחֵל","xlit":"Râchêl","gloss":"Rachel, a wife of Jacob","kjv":"Rachel","count":15,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","xlit":"tsôʼn","gloss":"a collective name for a flock","kjv":"cattle, flock, lamb, sheep","count":17,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H3812","lemma":"לֵאָה","xlit":"Lêʼâh","gloss":"Leah, a wife of Jacob","kjv":"Leah","count":9,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H5348","lemma":"נָקֹד","xlit":"nâqôd","gloss":"spotted","kjv":"speckled","count":7,"share":0.07}],"verses":["Gen.24.29","Gen.28.5","Gen.29.13","Gen.29.14","Gen.29.15","Gen.29.16","Gen.29.19","Gen.29.21","Gen.29.22","Gen.29.24","Gen.29.25","Gen.29.26","Gen.29.29","Gen.30.27","Gen.30.34","Gen.30.36","Gen.30.40","Gen.30.42","Gen.31.1","Gen.31.2","Gen.31.12","Gen.31.19","Gen.31.20","Gen.31.22","Gen.31.24","Gen.31.25","Gen.31.26","Gen.31.31","Gen.31.33","Gen.31.34","Gen.31.36","Gen.31.43","Gen.31.47","Gen.31.48","Gen.31.51","Gen.31.55","Gen.22.23","Gen.24.15","Gen.24.30","Gen.24.31","Gen.24.32","Gen.24.33","Gen.29.12","Gen.29.17","Gen.29.18","Gen.29.20","Gen.29.23","Gen.29.27","Gen.29.28","Gen.29.30","Gen.30.28","Gen.30.29","Gen.30.30","G